<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TIER 2 — an expanded context surface: the Display popover, the Objects panel,
  the start chooser's panel.

  Opaque, because it carries a body of content that has to be READ rather than
  glanced at, and borderless for the same reason Tier 1 is: one step of tone and
  a soft shadow are what separate it from the model, and an outline on a panel
  this size reads as a dialog frame.

  A 1 dp HAIRLINE (`UI-CRAFT-R1`). Tone and a soft shadow alone left a
  translucent surface over a rendered model reading as a smudge rather than
  as an edge; the hairline, in the palette's own fsChromeHairline, is what
  every precision tool draws around a floating panel and is what makes the
  surface's corner crisp. It is a hairline and never a frame: 1 dp, at the
  low contrast the role was approved at.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="?attr/fsSurfaceContext" />
    <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_floating" />
    <stroke
        android:width="@dimen/control_border_width"
        android:color="?attr/fsChromeHairline" />
</shape>
